Let the bottom-left corner be \(D=(0,0)\), bottom-right \(A=(10,0)\), top-left \(C=(0,8)\), top-right \(B=(10,8)\).  
From the grid, \(P=(0,4)\), and after bouncing off the left side the ball travels with direction \((1,1)\) at \(45^\circ\).

Track the rebounds:
\[
(0,4)\xrightarrow{\ \ }
(4,8)\quad\text{(top wall)}
\]
\[
(4,8)\xrightarrow{\ \ }
(10,2)\quad\text{(right wall)}
\]
\[
(10,2)\xrightarrow{\ \ }
(8,0)\quad\text{(bottom wall)}
\]
\[
(8,0)\xrightarrow{\ \ }
(0,8)=C.
\]
The bottom pocket \(E\) is at \((5,0)\), so it is not hit; none of the earlier wall hits are pockets. Hence the ball falls into pocket \(C\).

\[
\boxed{\text{C: Pocket C}}
\]
